%T A401316 21117612
%N A401316 Number of self-avoiding lattice paths from (0,0) to (n,n) in an n X n square grid such that no two maximal straight segments have equal length.
%C A401316 a(0) = 1 counts the trivial path from (0,0) to itself.
%C A401316 For n > 0, a(n) is a multiple of 4: a solution cannot have symmetry across y=x or y=n-x or it would contain two segments of equal length along different axes, and it cannot have 180-degree rotational symmetry or its first and last segments would have equal length.
%e A401316 For n=7, one solution is:
%e A401316 *   *   *---*---*---*---*---E
%e A401316         |
%e A401316 *   *   *   *---*---*---*---*
%e A401316         |   |               |
%e A401316 *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *
%e A401316         |   |               |
%e A401316 *   *   *---*   *   *   *   *
%e A401316                             |
%e A401316 *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *
%e A401316                             |
%e A401316 *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *
%e A401316                             |
%e A401316 *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *
%e A401316                             |
%e A401316 S---*---*---*---*---*---*---*
%e A401316 Here S=(0,0) and E=(7,7). Its successive straight-segment lengths are 7,6,4,2,1,3,5 which include no repeated lengths.
%Y A401316 Cf. A007764, A265132, A400112 (constraint only applied to consecutive segments).
%K A401316 nonn,walk,nice,hard,more,new
%O A401316 0,4
